Networking Documentation

Project Environment

- Cloud Platform: Amazon Web Services (AWS)
- Service: EC2
- Operating System: Ubuntu Linux
- Network Access: SSH

1. IP Addressing

IP addresses identify devices on a network.

Commands practiced:

ip addr
hostname -I

- Private IP: Used for communication within the AWS network.
- Public IP: Used to access the EC2 instance over the internet.

2. DNS

DNS (Domain Name System) translates domain names into IP addresses.

Commands:

ping -c 4 google.com
nslookup google.com

3. Network Ports

Port| Protocol / Service
22| SSH
80| HTTP
443| HTTPS
3306| MySQL
8080| Alternative Web Service

4. Listening Ports

Command:

sudo ss -tuln

This command displays network sockets and listening ports.

5. AWS Security Groups

Security Groups act as virtual firewalls for EC2 instances.

Example inbound rules:

Type| Port| Purpose
SSH| 22| Secure server access
HTTP| 80| Web traffic

SSH access should be restricted to the administrator's IP address.

Learning Outcomes

Practiced basic networking commands, IP address identification, DNS resolution, port inspection, and AWS Security Group concepts.
